{"records":[{"id":"hx4nwr8yyd","title":"Data for: Therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia developing 14 years after allogeneic stem cell transplantation, from a persistent R882H-DNMT3A mutated clone of patient origin.","description":"Supplementary (DOCX  2.34MB): \nMaterials and methods. \nFig. S1. TP53 mutation found in the lung carcinoma cells taken from the patient in 2012. \nFig. S2. Karyotype illustrating the metaphases of the 2015 therapy-related myelodysplastic syndrome cells. \nFig. S3. Paint of chromosome 15 (green) by fluorescent in situ hybridization. \nFig. S4. Analysis of the chimerism (Mentype® Chimera® software, Biotype) at 2015 therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis. \nFig. S5. IDH1, DNMT3A and NPM1 mutations found at the time of the acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis in 2001. \nFig. S6. DNMT3A and TP53 mutations found at the time of the therapy-related acute myeloid leukemia diagnosis in 2015. \nFig. S7. Standard curve for the ASO-qPCR. \nFig. S8. Sensitivity assay for quantitative ASO-qPCR. \n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-07-18T12:28:12.179Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hx4nwr8yyd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hx4nwr8yyd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Iván","last_name":"Martín","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Felipe J","last_name":"Chaves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rosario","last_name":"Abellán","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Francisca","last_name":"García","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mar","last_name":"Tormo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Carlos","last_name":"Solano","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Juan-Carlos","last_name":"Hernandez-Boluda","orcid":null},{"first_name":"María Dolores","last_name":"Olivares","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Eva","last_name":"Villamón","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Fernando","last_name":"Domingo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Blanca","last_name":"Navarro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marisa","last_name":"Calabuig","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Paula","last_name":"Amat","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alicia","last_name":"Serrano","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Cytogenetics"],"journal_issn":["00144800"]},{"id":"7tzk9r4mn8","title":"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia_2","description":"This dataset contains the raw FACS data of in vivo experiments without CART or AML used to generate the Figures in the paper titled \"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-08-20T06:12:09.186Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7tzk9r4mn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7tzk9r4mn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"ying","last_name":"zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ruijin","last_name":"Ji","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Hematopoietic Stem Cell","Acute Leukemia"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"774twr6fb8","title":"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia_1","description":"This dataset contains the raw FACS data of in vitro experiments used to generate the Figures in the paper titled \"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia\".\n\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-08-20T06:12:09.566Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/774twr6fb8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/774twr6fb8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"ying","last_name":"zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ruijin","last_name":"Ji","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Hematopoietic Stem Cell","Acute Leukemia"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"bs3r484nfn","title":"Anti-leukemic properties of aplysinopsin derivative EE-84 alone and in combination with BH3 mimetic A-1210477 (2)","description":"Aplysinopsins are a class of marine indole alkaloids that exhibit a wide range of biological activities such as prevention of neoplastic growth on an array of different cancer cell lines. Although both the indole and N-benzyl moieties of aplysinopsins are known to possess anti-proliferative activity against cancer cells, their mechanism of action remains unclear. Through in vitro and in vivo proliferation and viability screening of newly synthesized aplysinopsin analogs on myelogenous leukemia cell lines and zebrafish toxicity tests as well as analysis of differential toxicity in non-cancerous RPMI 1788 cells, we identified EE-84 as a promising novel drug candidate against myeloid leukemia. This indole derivative demonstrated drug-likeness in agreement with Lipinski’s rule of five and was responsible for cell cycle dysregulation in K562 cells in line with its cytostatic effect. EE-84-treated K562 cells likewise underwent morphological changes suggesting mitochondrial dysfunction. Finally, we demonstrated the synergistic cytotoxic effect of EE-84 with a BH3 mimetic, the Mcl-1 inhibitor, A-1210477, against K562 cells, highlighting the inhibition of anti-apoptotic Bcl-2 proteins as a promising therapeutic approach against myeloid leukemia in combination with EE-84. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-12-14T02:02:37.268Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bs3r484nfn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bs3r484nfn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Su A","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Health Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"z2rkrgwbm9","title":"Anti-leukemic properties of aplysinopsin derivative EE-84 alone and in combination with BH3 mimetic A-1210477","description":"Aplysinopsins are a class of marine indole alkaloids that exhibit a wide range of biological activities such as prevention of neoplastic growth on an array of different cancer cell lines. Although both the indole and N-benzyl moieties of aplysinopsins are known to possess anti-proliferative activity against cancer cells, their mechanism of action remains unclear. Through in vitro and in vivo proliferation and viability screening of newly synthesized aplysinopsin analogs on myelogenous leukemia cell lines and zebrafish toxicity tests as well as analysis of differential toxicity in non-cancerous RPMI 1788 cells and PBMCs, we identified EE-84 as a promising novel drug candidate against myeloid leukemia. This indole derivative demonstrated drug-likeness in agreement with Lipinski’s rule of five and was responsible for the senescent-like phenotype in K562 cells in line with its cytostatic effect. EE-84-treated K562 cells likewise underwent morphological changes suggesting mitochondrial dysfunction, autophagy and ER stress as cellular stress responses. Finally, we demonstrated the synergistic cytotoxic effect of EE-84 with a BH3 mimetic, the Mcl-1 inhibitor (A-1210477), against K562 and K562IR cells, highlighting the inhibition of anti-apoptotic Bcl-2 proteins as a promising therapeutic approach against chronic myeloid leukemia. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-01-20T19:05:27.903Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/z2rkrgwbm9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/z2rkrgwbm9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Su A","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Health Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"pbyjckj6g9","title":"SABRE HP Pyruvate Fluxomics in Mammalian Cells (U937 AML and Glial)","description":"Raw and processed data showing first results of SABRE hyperpolarized (HP) benchtop NMR fluxomics in U937 acute myeloid leukemia (AML) and glial cells, as well as general demonstrations of the technique details and technique flexibility.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-04-03T15:33:21.249Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pbyjckj6g9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pbyjckj6g9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Patrick","last_name":"TomHon","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metabolism","Hyperpolarization","Hyperpolarized Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy","In Vitro Study","Fluxomics","13C NMR Spectroscopy"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kd9bjf244c","title":"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia_3","description":"This dataset contains the raw FACS data of in vivo experiments with CART or AML used to generate the Figures in the paper titled \"Precision Epitope-engineering in Hematopoietic Stem and Progenitor Cells enables CD123 CAR-T cell immunotherapy for acute myeloid leukemia\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-08-20T06:10:41.36Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kd9bjf244c","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kd9bjf244c"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"ying","last_name":"zhang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Hematopoietic Stem Cell","Acute Leukemia"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fz7d6x4bwx","title":"Artificial Intelligence Reveals the Predictions of Hematological Indexes in Children with Acute Leukemia","description":"Childhood leukemia is a prevalent form of pediatric cancer, with acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) being the primary manifestations. Timely treatment has significantly enhanced survival rates for children with acute leukemia. This study aimed to develop an early and comprehensive predictor for hematologic malignancies in children by examining nutritional markers, key leukemia indicators, and granulocytes in patients' blood. Using a machine learning algorithm and ten indices, 826 pediatric patients with ALL and 255 children with AML were analyzed, comparing them with a control group of 200 healthy children. The study revealed notable differences, including higher indicators in boys compared to girls and significant variations in most biochemical indicators between leukemia patients and healthy children. Employing a random forest model resulted in an Area Under the Curve (AUC) of 0.950 for predicting leukemia subtypes and an AUC of 0.909 for forecasting AML. This research introduces an efficient diagnostic tool for early screening of childhood blood cancers and underscores the potential of artificial intelligence in modern healthcare.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-02-11T03:29:59.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fz7d6x4bwx","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fz7d6x4bwx"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Haiyang","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coding in Methodology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"48s882jvnr","title":"Case report-CARE Checklist","description":"Care checklist for case report-Metachronous Presentation of BCL2-Positive Lung Adenocarcinoma and Acute Myeloid Leukemia: a case presentation and review of the literature","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-04-28T08:34:58.817Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/48s882jvnr","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/48s882jvnr"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Bo","last_name":"Zheng","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Data Access"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ym9mcsm2fg","title":"Anti-leukemic properties of aplysinopsin derivative EE-84 alone and in combination with BH3 mimetic A-1210477 (3)","description":"Aplysinopsins are a class of marine indole alkaloids that exhibit a wide range of biological activities such as prevention of neoplastic growth on an array of different cancer cell lines. Although both the indole and N-benzyl moieties of aplysinopsins are known to possess anti-proliferative activity against cancer cells, their mechanism of action remains unclear. Through in vitro and in vivo proliferation and viability screening of newly synthesized aplysinopsin analogs on myelogenous leukemia cell lines and zebrafish toxicity tests as well as analysis of differential toxicity in non-cancerous RPMI 1788 cells and PBMCs, we identified EE-84 as a promising novel drug candidate against myeloid leukemia. This indole derivative demonstrated drug-likeness in agreement with Lipinski’s rule of five and was responsible for the senescent-like phenotype in K562 cells in line with its cytostatic effect. EE-84-treated K562 cells likewise underwent morphological changes suggesting mitochondrial dysfunction, autophagy and ER stress as cellular stress responses. Finally, we demonstrated the synergistic cytotoxic effect of EE-84 with a BH3 mimetic, the Mcl-1 inhibitor (A-1210477), against K562 and K562IR cells, highlighting the inhibition of anti-apoptotic Bcl-2 proteins as a promising therapeutic approach against chronic myeloid leukemia. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-01-19T13:27:50.252Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ym9mcsm2fg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ym9mcsm2fg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Su A","last_name":"Kim","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Health Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":147676,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":198,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":147676,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":146742,"restricted":74,"embargoed":860},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2384},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1399},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":719},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":484},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":458},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":445},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":429},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":407},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":339},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":285}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":144987},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1920},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":189},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":144},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":81},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":66},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":59},{"id":"b121dfec-bb51-4f19-a2f6-bc9ce0197286","name":"Babeș-Bolyai University","count":44},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":32},{"id":"f2ed6517-7fb4-4e02-8cef-95e75e9f0c9d","name":"Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University","count":28}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"ecb64011-71f0-5223-b4e4-4d27d5f51d83","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa","count":904},{"id":"9d63ad1d-c391-5c35-a12e-cafe17017098","name":"Universidad Autonoma de Madrid","count":874},{"id":"3bfef41a-d03e-5722-bd55-dd245235fa78","name":"Bina Nusantara University","count":554},{"id":"0ad97c43-5173-56e6-bbe6-46dad5323862","name":"Daffodil International University","count":411},{"id":"55ba66b2-f276-5204-a3d8-acfa499794e0","name":"The University of Manchester","count":395}]}}